-- title:
--   Hecke multiplier, width identity and supersingularity on α-fibres
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, a level $N\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$, subject to $N\ne 0$ in $K$, $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\ne p$. Write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`, and $R=$ `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ`, generated by `jqModC K`, `jqNModC K N`, `jqNModC K ℓ` and `jqNModC K (N*ℓ)`; let $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaC K N ℓ` (the inclusion $F\subseteq R$) and $\beta=$ `heckeBetaC K N ℓ` (the $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ degeneracy embedding), assumed integral via hypotheses `hα`, `hβ`. Let $x$ be a place of $F$ over $K$ (a proper valuation subring containing $K$ and a principal ideal ring) satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace p N K`, and let $S$ be a finite set of places of $R$ characterised by the hypothesis that $y\in S$ if and only if the restriction of $y$ along $\alpha$ equals $x$, i.e. $S$ is the $\alpha$-fibre over $x$. Then for every $y\in S$, writing $e_\alpha(y),e_\beta(y)$ for the ramification indices along $\alpha,\beta$, $y_\beta$ for the restriction of $y$ along $\beta$, $r=$ `placeRamificationJ N` and $u=$ `placeWidth N`: (i) the order at $y$ of the Hecke multiplier `heckeMultiplier N K ℓ` (the element $h\in R$ chosen to satisfy $d(\beta\,\bar\jmath)=h\cdot\alpha^{*}d\bar\jmath$ for the generator `jGeomGen K N`) equals $e_\beta(y)\,r(y_\beta)-e_\alpha(y)\,r(x)$; (ii) $e_\alpha(y)\,u(y_\beta)=e_\beta(y)\,u(x)$; and (iii) $y_\beta$ is again a supersingular place.
--
--   This packages the local behaviour at a supersingular place of the two degeneracy legs of the $\ell$-Hecke correspondence in characteristic $p$: the divisor of the multiplier comparing the pulled-back differentials of the $j$-coordinate, the compatibility of ramification indices with the widths of the places, and the preservation of supersingularity under $\ell$-isogeny. It is invoked as a single hypothesis package by the results establishing additivity and semilinearity properties of the supersingular Hecke operator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_SSHeckeV2_ord_heckeMultiplier_eq_and_width_eq_and_mem_ssPlaces_of_mem_fiber.lean

